{
  "summary": "This PR removes default construction and the public `Init()` method from `PrecomputedTransactionData`, requiring transaction and spent-output context at construction time. Validation and test call sites that require deferred precomputation now hold an `std::optional<PrecomputedTransactionData>` and emplace it only after script-cache misses. In `ConnectBlock()`, txdata vector allocation is skipped entirely when script checks are bypassed under assumevalid, and `btck_script_pubkey_verify()` in the kernel C API is fixed to avoid copying caller-supplied txdata on every call.",
  "problem": "Allowing `PrecomputedTransactionData` to exist without transaction data enabled an error-prone reuse path where cached BIP143 and BIP341 sighash data could theoretically carry over across transactions. Furthermore, the kernel verification C API inadvertently copied caller-supplied precomputed txdata on every invocation due to a ternary expression mixing lvalues and prvalues, and block connection needlessly allocated txdata memory during assumevalid verification.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit ffc8cf187b provides a compiler reproducer (Godbolt link) demonstrating that GCC copied caller-supplied `PrecomputedTransactionData` on every kernel script verification call prior to the fix.",
    "PR description highlights that the previous `Init()` check only asserted `!m_spent_outputs_ready`, leaving state tracking incomplete after forced initialization without spent outputs."
  ],
